 "session_ne": "दोस्रो",
 "summary": "The main purpose of the Asset Laundering (Money Laundering) Prevention (Third Amendment) Act, 2083 is to make the investigation and prosecution regarding money laundering more effective (Explanatory Note, Page 1). According to this Act, if a matter relating to money laundering is not related to a predicate offence, it shall be under the Department (Section 2, Page 2). Regarding submitting the report after completion of an investigation, in the case of the Department, it shall be submitted to the government attorney office designated by the Attorney General by publishing a notice in the Nepal Gazette, and in the case of others, to the concerned government attorney office (Section 3, Page 2). This Act shall come into force immediately (Section 1, Subsection 2, Page 2).\n\nThis Act repeals the Asset Laundering (Money Laundering) Prevention (Third Amendment) Ordinance, 2083 (Section 4, Subsection 1, Page 2). The cases relating to money laundering already registered in the Special Court pursuant to the Asset Laundering (Money Laundering) Prevention (Third Amendment) Ordinance, 2083 shall not be barred from being processed, heard, and disposed of by the same court (Section 4, Subsection 2, Page 2).",
